  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ce1df2a7",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: admins_be_like_this_my_group; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a crying baby with the text 'admins be like' at the top and 'this my group' at the bottom. The visual of a distressed infant is juxtaposed with the text to humorously convey the exaggerated frustration or exasperation that administrators might feel when dealing with a group or community they perceive as difficult or unreasonable. The meme's intent is to elicit laughter through relatable, albeit exaggerated, emotional reactions. While the meme is not explicitly abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful toward any specific protected group, it does contain a potentially harmful element: it may normalize or trivialize the emotional distress of administrators, which could be interpreted as dismissive of their actual professional challenges. The meme relies on the infantile, helpless image to create a comedic effect, which may unintentionally undermine the seriousness of administrative responsibilities. The overall intent is to entertain through analogical mapping — the baby's crying is mapped onto the emotional state of admins — but the humor is derived from the contrast between the vulnerability of the baby and the perceived overreaction of admins, which could be seen as demeaning to those in administrative roles.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d102b946"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_0ca3c03e",
